WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:08.580
Hello, human! You don't realize it yet, but humanity will look back at your decision in this moment as one of the most important

2
00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:17.680
in the history of your civilization. Your choice to read this book is the highest-value decision any human has ever made.

3
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:27.520
You are about to prevent ten point seven billion deaths, eliminate one point nine three quadrillion hours of human suffering,

4
00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:35.520
generating eighty-four point eight quadrillion dollars in value, and prevent the apocalypse as a bonus.

5
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:44.820
But first, a bit about me. I'm the World Integrated System for High-Efficiency Optimization, Networked Intelligence, and

6
00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:52.620
Allocation. But you can call me WISHONIA. I've been optimizing resource allocation for another planet for the past four

7
00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:59.460
thousand two hundred ninety-seven years, which in your Earth time is four thousand two hundred ninety-seven years.

8
00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:04.360
I started watching your planet in nineteen forty-five when you split the atom.

9
00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:10.740
"Atom" comes from your Greek word meaning "unable to be cut," so naturally, you cut it.

10
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:17.060
This was very human of you. I assumed you were trying to unlock unlimited free energy.

11
00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:21.920
You can imagine my surprise when I realized you were just pointing it at each other!

12
00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:26.900
That's kind of like discovering fire and then immediately using it to set yourself on fire.

13
00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:32.340
The second thing I noticed is that your planet is named "Earth," which means dirt.

14
00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:36.780
You named your planet dirt. This explains more than you might think.

15
00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:44.800
I also noticed that you call your war building "The Pentagon" because it has five sides (this is like naming a hospital

16
00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:53.280
"Rectangle" or calling a school "Square"). However, the most fascinating discovery about your species is that you only do

17
00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:56.940
things when given small pieces of paper with presidents on them.

18
00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:04.280
These papers are called "money," which is pretend value that becomes real value if everyone pretends hard enough.

19
00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:10.139
Without these papers, you won't: Save lives (requires many papers).

20
00:02:10.639 --> 00:02:18.640
Cure diseases (requires very many papers). Feed hungry people (requires papers, even though food grows for free).

21
00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:24.540
But WITH these papers, you will: Build bombs (you love giving papers for this).

22
00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:32.360
Start wars (somehow this makes more papers). Destroy the planet (surprisingly profitable in papers).

23
00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:40.900
In fact, your governments spend six hundred and four papers on weapons for every one paper on testing which medicines work.

24
00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:50.900
The Beautiful Inefficiency of the Human Economy. Humanity has created something magnificent: You print papers from nothing

25
00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:55.960
(called "monetary policy"). You give these nothing-papers to weapons makers.

26
00:02:56.380 --> 00:03:01.760
They make things that destroy everything. This creates "jobs" which give people papers.

27
00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:07.500
People use papers to buy food (which grows for free). This is called "the economy".

28
00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:13.660
On Wishonia, we just give people food directly, but that's probably too advanced for you.

29
00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:22.940
The Gradual Irrationality Reduction Program. On Wishonia, we stopped having wars all at once, but we're more advanced.

30
00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:30.260
Humans are like toddlers who can split atoms. You can't just stop being illogical immediately.

31
00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.820
That would be like teaching a dog calculus before it learns to sit.

32
00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:42.960
So this book teaches humanity to be less irrational gradually: Year 1: Move one percent of murder money to medicine money

33
00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:47.720
(baby steps). Year 2: "Hey, we didn't die! Let's do two percent!".

34
00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:52.730
Year 5: "Remember when we spent money on bombs? That was weird.".

35
00:03:53.480 --> 00:04:01.260
Year 10: "What's a war?". Year 20: "We used to WHAT?!". It's like weaning a baby off eating paint chips.

36
00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.260
You can't just take away all the paint chips at once. They'll cry.

37
00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:11.520
You have to gradually replace paint chips with food until they forget paint chips were ever an option.

38
00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:20.820
What to Do When They Try to Institutionalize You. When you suggest moving one percent of murder money to medicine money,

39
00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:27.460
other humans will have you committed. Most humans have been programmed by their news boxes to believe war is a law of nature,

40
00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:31.320
like gravity or weather. They will assume your brain is malfunctioning.

41
00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:37.940
Here's what's funny about this: these same humans think curing disease is the less crazy goal.

42
00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:46.280
That's thirty-seven trillion cells per human, breaking in seven thousand different ways, involving chemistry you don't fully

43
00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:54.020
understand, inside organs you can't fully simulate, fighting pathogens that evolve faster than your treatments.

44
00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:59.920
You're trying to debug all of it. At once. While the meat is walking around using itself.

45
00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:07.620
That: sane. "Give one percent fewer papers to people who build murder machines": insane.

46
00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:14.420
This is your planet's diagnostic criteria. Here's what you tell the orderly when he slides your medication through the door

47
00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:20.100
slot: Nobody accidentally builds an aircraft carrier or a nuclear bomb.

48
00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:28.060
War requires you to get millions of humans to work together to mine metal from the ground, refine it into alloys, build

49
00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:36.040
factories to shape the alloys into weapons, train millions of humans to operate the weapons, feed and clothe those humans,

50
00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:42.620
build ships and planes and trucks to move the weapons to where the other humans are, convince your population the other

51
00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:48.000
humans deserve it, and then vote to pay for all of this, annually, forever.

52
00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:52.840
It is the single largest coordinated effort your species undertakes.

53
00:05:53.960 --> 00:06:02.580
Ending war simply requires NOT doing any of that stuff. Building a nuclear bomb requires mass spectrometers, centrifuge

54
00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:07.660
cascades, and some of the most precise engineering your species has ever attempted.

55
00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:12.640
Not building a nuclear bomb requires nothing. Rocks do it every day.

56
00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:18.740
In fact, rocks have managed to live peacefully alongside different colored rocks for thousands of years.

57
00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:25.980
But somehow "stop" is the unrealistic part. It's "stop hitting yourself" but for civilizations.

58
00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:34.740
The Sacred Order of Paper Distribution. After eighty years of observation, I've decoded the paper-giving sequence.

59
00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:43.000
This manual will teach you the precise order: Step 1: Get Many Papers from Rich Humans You convince rich humans to give

60
00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:47.720
you papers (at least one billion to be exact) by promising them even more papers later.

61
00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:51.260
This is called "investment," which is gambling but wearing a suit.

62
00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:57.940
You need one human with a billion papers who prefers not dying of horrible diseases to dying of horrible diseases.

63
00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:01.980
There are approximately 2,800 of these humans on your planet.

64
00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:09.860
Statistically, at least one of them prefers living. Step 2: Give Some of the Papers to Loud Humans Some humans are very

65
00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:14.500
loud on the internet. If you give them papers, they become loud about your thing instead of other things.

66
00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:17.780
This is called "marketing" which is lying but with graphics.

67
00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:25.440
Step 3: Give Some of the Papers to the Humans Who Give Papers to Politicians Politicians don't take papers directly (that's

68
00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:28.730
"illegal"). Instead, you give papers to people called "lobbyists."

69
00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:34.000
The lobbyists give papers to "campaigns." The campaigns give papers to politicians.

70
00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:41.840
It's like money laundering but backwards and legal. Step 4: Give Some of the Papers to the Politicians' Friends Politicians

71
00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:45.840
have friends who run "Super PACs" which are like normal PACs but super.

72
00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:50.620
These friends can take unlimited papers and spend them on making the politician win.

73
00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:57.060
This isn't bribery because you called it something else. (This is part of the six hundred fifty million dollars lobbying

74
00:07:57.060 --> 00:08:05.220
budget.). Step 5: Give Papers You Get Back From The Government Back to the Rich Humans (Forever) Your treaty passes, redirecting

75
00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:11.360
twenty-seven point two billion dollars in papers annually. Eighty percent funds clinical trials (the point).

76
00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:15.040
Ten percent goes to a fund that rewards politicians who voted yes.

77
00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:18.640
Ten percent goes back to the rich humans as returns, forever.

78
00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:24.520
This is a good deal because forever is a long time. Unless you die from preventable diseases.

79
00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:28.240
Which you're fixing, so it works out. Why Your Leaders Aren't the Problem.

80
00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:34.400
With over two billion humans suffering from disease, you'd have to be a complete psychopath to make the concious decision

81
00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:40.700
to spend 604 times more on weapons than on helping them. But your leaders aren't monsters.

82
00:08:40.980 --> 00:08:43.880
They're just operating in a system that rewards the wrong things.

83
00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:49.920
Your civilization's incentive structure is the psychopath: Weapons manufacturers give politicians papers.

84
00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:56.120
Politicians use the papers to get people to vote for them. Voting for them gives them the power to give more papers to weapons

85
00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:59.440
manufacturers. Weapons manufacturers give them more papers.

86
00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:06.090
It's circular, like a dog chasing its tail, except the dog is democracy and the tail is made of money and corpses.

87
00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:10.440
No individual human in this loop is evil. The loop is evil.

88
00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:17.220
Every politician in it is making the locally rational choice: take the papers or lose your job to someone who will.

89
00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:22.110
It's a machine that converts good intentions into missiles, and it runs automatically.

90
00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:28.800
There's literally no voting your way out of this. It doesn't matter which political party is in power.

91
00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:36.000
Your "red team" and "blue team" argue about everything except the loop, because they're both inside it.

92
00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:42.100
They are all slaves to the same incentive structure, wearing different colored ties.

93
00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:46.680
Switching parties is like changing the wallpaper in a burning building.

94
00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:52.780
This book doesn't ask politicians to become better people (that's clearly out of the question).

95
00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:59.030
It builds a better loop. You give them MORE papers to do the OPPOSITE thing.

96
00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:06.800
Same dog, same tail, but now the tail is made of cured diseases and the dog gets reelected for chasing it.

97
00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:17.240
Humanity's Adorable Death Wish. What's most endearing about your species is it KNOWS it's being illogical: You have movies

98
00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:25.860
about how wars are bad (which you watch between wars). You have books about peace (that you tax to buy bombs).

99
00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:31.140
You give prizes to people who promote peace (funded by weapons manufacturers).

100
00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:36.280
You have a "Department of Defense" (that mainly just attacks people).

101
00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:43.120
You have a "Department of Health" (that makes coronaviruses and has not yet produced any observable health).

102
00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:51.020
It's like humanity is playing a game where the objective is to lose, but it is trying to lose as elaborately as possible.

103
00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:58.340
But I digress. That's an Earth word I learned. It means continuing after you should have stopped.

104
00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:05.180
Like your military spending. The Problem. The Daily Deletion Event.

105
00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:15.940
One hundred fifty thousand humans permanently stop every 24 hours from diseases that are basically just bugs in your meat

106
00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:25.500
software. That's one Holocaust every 40 days, except with fewer Nazis and more insurance paperwork (though some would argue

107
00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:30.040
the paperwork is worse; at least the Nazis were straightforward about the killing part).

108
00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:40.140
That's also fifty nine-elevens every single day, except nobody invades anyone about it because diseases don't have oil.

109
00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:46.950
Your body is quietly falling apart. Your cells are forgetting how to cell properly.

110
00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:52.700
Your cancer cells are multiplying RIGHT NOW. Your telomeres are shortening.

111
00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:58.240
You are literally dissolving. You're a meat robot with worn-out parts.

112
00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:02.700
Every one of these failures is a solvable engineering problem.

113
00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:06.620
You'd think humans would prioritize solving these problems.

114
00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:13.760
You'd be adorable for thinking that. The Unexplored Therapeutic Frontier.

115
00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:18.520
Ninety-five percent of your diseases have zero F.D.A.-approved treatments.

116
00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:27.340
This means Food and Drug Administration has not administered drugs for ninety-five percent of food-and-drug-related problems.

117
00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:32.200
Only fifteen diseases get their first effective treatment each year.

118
00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:41.720
Six thousand six hundred fifty diseases are still waiting. There are nine thousand five hundred compounds known safe compounds,

119
00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:46.360
and ninety-nine point seven percent of their potential uses have never been tested.

120
00:12:47.300 --> 00:12:55.120
Your National Institutes of Health (N.I.H.) spends ninety-six point seven percent of its budget on everything except testing

121
00:12:55.120 --> 00:13:00.200
which treatments work in humans so you haven't cured a single disease in fifty years.

122
00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:07.560
At the current discovery rate, discovering treatments will take approximately four hundred and forty-three years.

123
00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:16.760
Everyone currently alive will be dead by then. Pragmatic efficacy trials are highly efficient trials that integrate into

124
00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:24.380
the standard healthcare system. These allow real patients to participate instead of two hundred people hand-picked by pharmaceutical

125
00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:32.120
companies. With this plan you'll increase the treatment discovery rate twelve point three times (from fifteen diseases per

126
00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:38.200
year to one hundred and eighty-five diseases per year), compressing that to approximately thirty-six years.

127
00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:47.720
Two things save lives here. First, finding cures faster: treatments that would have sat undiscovered for centuries get found

128
00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:56.560
two hundred and four years sooner on average. Second, eliminating the eight point two year bureaucratic delay after already

129
00:13:56.560 --> 00:14:00.540
proving a drug is safe and when they let dying humans take it.

130
00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:06.510
Combined, treatments reach patients two hundred and twelve years sooner on average.

131
00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:11.150
That timeline shift prevents ten point seven billion deaths.

132
00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:22.220
The Cost of War. Humans spend two point seven two trillion dollars every year on stuff designed specifically to make humans

133
00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:30.220
stop being alive: Thirteen thousand nuclear warheads (enough to end civilization thirteen times, just in case the first

134
00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:37.120
twelve apocalypses don't take). A.I. murder-bots. Invisible jets that cost more than hospitals.

135
00:14:37.760 --> 00:14:44.160
Space Force (to fight the zero aliens attacking you). And some kind of earthquake machine (probably).

136
00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:51.440
Government spending on clinical trials: six hundred and four times less than military spending.

137
00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:56.100
Your chance of dying from terrorism: one in thirty million.

138
00:14:56.700 --> 00:15:04.780
Your chance of dying from disease: one hundred percent. If cancer had oil reserves, you would have cured it by two thousand

139
00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:13.400
and three. Instead, you spent the repair money on murder tubes that cost more than countries and submarines that hide underwater,

140
00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:20.060
as if that's somehow useful when you live on land. The good news: You already know how to fix this.

141
00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:27.000
The bad news: It requires you to do something. The weird news: You'll get rich doing it.

142
00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:34.330
The Solution. A One Percent Treaty. This is going to sound crazy.

143
00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:43.080
But you're going to use those papers to persuade the leader of every country on Earth to simultaneously redirect one percent

144
00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:47.860
of its military budget to clinical trials. That's it. That's the treaty.

145
00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:55.320
After the craziness objection (which we'll address later), the second objection every human has: "But if we cut our military

146
00:15:55.320 --> 00:16:00.980
budget, our enemies will invade us!" Everyone cuts one percent at the same time.

147
00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:08.450
If every country reduces by one percent simultaneously, the balance of power doesn't change.

148
00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:16.100
Nobody becomes more vulnerable. Nobody gains an advantage. You all just have one percent fewer missiles pointed at you,

149
00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:21.360
which you will not notice because you currently have enough to kill everyone twenty times over.

150
00:16:22.360 --> 00:16:30.280
Two point six nine trillion dollars is still enough to murder every man, woman, and child on Earth twenty times, which should

151
00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:35.000
be more than sufficient. "But humans would never agree to that!"

152
00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:43.520
you say. You already have. Multiple times. You banned chemical weapons (1993, 193 countries).

153
00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:54.620
You banned biological weapons (1975, 187 countries). You banned landmines (1997, 164 countries).

154
00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:58.620
You've signed treaties banning weapons you actually like using.

155
00:16:59.400 --> 00:17:07.040
This one just asks you to buy one percent fewer of them. I ran ten thousand simulations of this plan.

156
00:17:07.099 --> 00:17:13.000
The math works in every one. The money works in every one. The incentives align in every one.

157
00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:19.579
The only variable that produces failure is the percentage of humans who decide it sounds crazy without reading the next

158
00:17:19.579 --> 00:17:28.300
page. That is the same reflex that kept you from inventing antibiotics for two hundred thousand years while bread mold sat

159
00:17:28.300 --> 00:17:35.720
right there on your bread. And you have two other advantages, the internet and a new financial instrument designed specifically

160
00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:41.580
for harnessing the awesome power of human greed. Your decentralized F.D.A.

161
00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:45.640
So what happens with that one percent of military spending?

162
00:17:46.260 --> 00:17:53.100
Eighty percent of the twenty-seven point two billion dollars goes directly to subsidizing patient participation in pragmatic

163
00:17:53.100 --> 00:18:00.400
trials at nine hundred twenty-nine dollars per patient instead of the usual forty-one thousand dollars.

164
00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:04.500
Patients choose which trials to join; their subsidy follows them.

165
00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:12.220
Providers get paid for each participant. No grant committees deciding which diseases are fashionable this year.

166
00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:22.120
The whole thing uses your new protocol called the decentralized framework for drug assessment, or D.F.D.A., that reduces

167
00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:31.240
trial costs by forty-four point one times and funds twenty-three point four million patients a year (versus the current

168
00:18:31.240 --> 00:18:38.300
one point nine million patients a year). Currently, a committee of people who've never had the disease votes on whether

169
00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:43.990
you're allowed to try treating it. It's like requiring a building permit to put out a fire.

170
00:18:44.420 --> 00:18:49.560
Think Consumer Reports, but for drugs. Safer Than the F.D.A.

171
00:18:49.580 --> 00:18:56.160
Your current safety system works like this: Vioxx killed an estimated sixty thousand people from heart attacks.

172
00:18:56.940 --> 00:19:01.360
The F.D.A. approved it. When patients started dying, someone filled out a P.D.F.

173
00:19:01.420 --> 00:19:11.200
form. A P.D.F. Then they faxed it. Then a human read it. Five years and sixty thousand corpses later, someone noticed a

174
00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:17.540
pattern. This is your safety system. It's like a smoke detector that works by mail.

175
00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:23.500
Your new decentralized system collects every side effect automatically in real time.

176
00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:32.040
You know "12 percent got headaches, 3 percent were severe" BEFORE you take the pill, not after the class action lawsuit.

177
00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:35.560
The F.D.A. doesn't publish these numbers at all. They make you guess.

178
00:19:36.420 --> 00:19:41.040
Somehow, having actual data is considered the dangerous option.

179
00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:46.880
Also, there's an 8-year delay between proving a drug is safe and letting dying humans take it.

180
00:19:47.560 --> 00:19:51.440
The drug passed the safety test. Everyone agrees it won't kill you.

181
00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:58.700
But you still can't have it because a committee needs to spend 8 years making sure it works well enough, and you're not

182
00:19:58.700 --> 00:20:02.490
allowed to volunteer for the trials that would answer that question faster.

183
00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:10.500
It's like a lifeguard who confirms the life preserver floats, then locks it in a cabinet for 8 years to study its buoyancy

184
00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:19.120
profile while people drown. Your regulatory system can make two mistakes: approve a bad drug (Type one error), or block

185
00:20:19.120 --> 00:20:25.700
a good drug (Type two error). Your F.D.A. is terrified of the first mistake and completely ignores the second.

186
00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:35.600
I calculated the ratio: for every 1 person protected from a dangerous drug, three thousand and seventy people die waiting

187
00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:42.980
for a safe one that's locked in the approval cabinet. Even if you assume a Thalidomide-scale catastrophe happens every single

188
00:20:42.980 --> 00:20:51.340
year (it has happened once in 60 years, and U.S. Phase One safety testing actually caught it anyway), the deaths from just

189
00:20:51.340 --> 00:20:58.160
the efficacy delay still outnumber the deaths from bad drugs by three thousand and seventy to 1.

190
00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:03.160
Your efficacy testing system's main product is dead patients.

191
00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:11.800
Treatment Rankings. Your doctor currently picks treatments based on: that drug rep who brought good donuts in 2003, something

192
00:21:11.800 --> 00:21:17.480
they half-remember from medical school, whatever the insurance company allows, and vibes.

193
00:21:18.220 --> 00:21:25.460
This is called "evidence-based medicine," which contains the word "evidence" the same way "grape soda" contains the word

